      "description": "Note: You can easily convert this markdown file to a PDF in VSCode using this handy extension Markdown PDF.\nBack to the Top\nComplex Programmable Logic Device (CPLD) is a combination of a fully programmable AND/OR array and a bank of macrocells. The AND/OR array is reprogrammable and can perform a multitude of logic functions. Macrocells are functional blocks that perform combinatorial or sequential logic, and also have the added flexibility for true or complement, along with varied feedback paths.\nProgrammable Logic Device (PLD) is an electrical component used to build reconfigurable digital circuits.Unlike integrated circuits (IC) which consist of logic gates and have a fixed function, a PLD has an undefined function at the time of manufacture.\nElectrically erasable programmable read-only memory (EEPROM) is a memory configuration stored in non-volatile memory and can be accessed even after a reboot.\nCentral Processing Unit (CPU) is a circuit that's composed of multiple cores that executes instructions comprising a computer program. The CPU performs basic arithmetic, logic, controlling, and input/output (I/O) operations specified by the instructions in the program. This is different from other external components such as main memory, I/O circuitry, and graphics processing units (GPUs).\nVector Processor is a central processing unit (CPU) that implements an instruction set where its instructions are designed to operate efficiently and effectively on large one-dimensional arrays of data called vectors.\nApplication Specific Integrated Circuits (ASICs) is an integrated circuit (IC) chip customized for a particular use in embedded systems, mobile phones, personal computers, professional workstations, rather than intended for general use.\nSingle Instruction, Multiple Data (SIMD) is a type of parallel processing that describes computers with multiple processing elements that perform the same operation on multiple data points simultaneously.\nWhat is CPLD (Complex Programmable Logic Device)? | Autodesk\nIntroduction to FPGA Design for Embedded Systems - CPLD Architecture | Coursera\nXilinx FPGA Training - Fundamentals of CPLD Design\nVLSI Course Series - FPGA Architecture Basics | Udemy\nIntel® FPGAs and Programmable Devices-Intel® FPGA",
